/-!
# Low-degree support vanishing for a relative smooth divisor

Source: `literature/blueprint/latest/blueprint/sec-smooth-purity/sk-prop-an/
lem-pur-divisor-class.proof.md`,
clause (b) (blueprint: lem-pur-smooth-divisor-low-support).

The theorem states the low-degree vanishing of the cohomology sheaves with support in a
smooth relative divisor.  The supported sheaf is the right-derived functor of the kernel
`F ↦ ker(F ⟶ j_*j^{-1}F)` from `AlgebraicGeometry.Etale.sectionsWithSupport`; its
cohomology sheaves are obtained with `DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor`.
-/

@[expose] public section
set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

open CategoryTheory Limits Opposite
open AlgebraicGeometry
open AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Etale

/-- Low-degree étale local-cohomology sheaves vanish for a smooth relative divisor.

Source: `literature/blueprint/latest/blueprint/sec-smooth-purity/sk-prop-an/
lem-pur-divisor-class.proof.md`,
clause (b) (blueprint: lem-pur-smooth-divisor-low-support).

The hypotheses say that `b : B ⟶ Spec k`, `v : T ⟶ B`, and the composite through the
closed immersion `i : D ⟶ T` are separated and finite type over `k`; `v` is smooth of
relative dimension `n`, `i ≫ v` is smooth, and the stalk Krull dimensions differ by one.
The coefficient ring is finite commutative, `ell` is prime and invertible in `k`, and
`ell ^ N` annihilates it.  For every integer `q < 2`, the `q`-th homology sheaf of the
right-derived supported-kernel functor applied to the finite étale Tate sheaf
`μ_(ell^N) ⊗ Λ` is zero. The statement includes the empty divisor and makes no regularity
or reducedness assumption on `B`.

Proof. The remaining local calculations are isolated in the standard-pair and chart-transport
statements imported above; the parent integer wrapper proceeds as follows.
1. The schemes are Noetherian of finite dimension, being finite type over a field.
   The smooth-pair coordinate lemma gives, near each point of `D`, an étale chart
   identifying the immersion with a coordinate subspace. Its ideal is generated by a
   regular sequence of length `b`. The dimension formula for its successive quotients
   gives dim O_T = dim O_D + b. The codimension hypothesis forces b = 1, so the pair
   is étale-locally the zero section of an affine line over a relative affine space.
2. For the standard pair s : Y → A¹_Y, let G = R(s^!₀)(Λ(1)). The supported-kernel
   adjunction identifies RP_s(Λ(1)) with s_*G, because closed direct image is exact.
   The closed-support triangle is s_*G → Λ(1) → Rj_*Λ(1) → s_*G[1]. Apply Rp_*,
   with p the affine-line projection and p ∘ s = id, to obtain
   G → Rp_*Λ(1) → Rπ_*Λ(1) → G[1], where π = p ∘ j.
3. The general-base relative-line low-degree lemma identifies p_*Λ(1) and π_*Λ(1)
   with Λ_Y(1), and identifies the intervening restriction with the identity. It also
   gives R¹p_*Λ(1) = 0. The cohomology sequence therefore gives H⁰G = H¹G = 0.
   Negative cohomology vanishes from the nonnegative injective resolution. Exactness
   of s_* gives H^q(RP_sΛ(1)) = 0 for all q < 2.
4. Étale restriction preserves injectives and commutes with the support kernel.
   The finite Tate pullback comparison identifies the restricted coefficient sheaf.
   Exact inverse image commutes with cohomology, so Step 3 applies on every chart
   from Step 1. Outside D the support kernel is zero. Conservative geometric stalks
   give vanishing on T; negative degrees again vanish by a nonnegative resolution.
   For D empty the support functor is identically zero. These computations retain
   the Λ-action, so they give the displayed vanishing of Λ-module sheaves.
5. The standard-pair calculation and its unbounded-to-Plus comparison are isolated in
   `isZero_homology_rightDerivedSectionsWithSupport_standard_pair`; Step 4 transports that
   calculation across the smooth étale charts in
   `isZero_homology_rightDerivedSectionsWithSupport_of_smooth_divisor_of_standard_pair`.
   Negative q are handled directly by the nonnegative bound for a right-derived functor
   applied to a degree-zero single object. For q >= 0, q < 2 is the required 0-or-1
   integer range, and the transport theorem supplies both degrees together.
-/
theorem isZero_homology_rightDerivedSectionsWithSupport_of_smooth_divisor
    {k : Type u} [Field k] (ell N : ℕ) (hell : Nat.Prime ell)
    (hell_unit : IsUnit (ell : k)) (hN : 1 ≤ N)
    {B T D : Scheme.{u}}
    (b : B ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [IsSeparated b] [LocallyOfFiniteType b] [QuasiCompact b]
    (v : T ⟶ B) (n : ℕ) [SmoothOfRelativeDimension n v]
    [IsSeparated (v ≫ b)] [LocallyOfFiniteType (v ≫ b)] [QuasiCompact (v ≫ b)]
    (i : D ⟶ T) [IsClosedImmersion i] [Smooth (i ≫ v)]
    [IsSeparated (i ≫ v ≫ b)] [LocallyOfFiniteType (i ≫ v ≫ b)]
    [QuasiCompact (i ≫ v ≫ b)]
    (hcodim : ∀ d : D, ringKrullDim (T.presheaf.stalk (i d)) =
      ringKrullDim (D.presheaf.stalk d) + (1 : WithBot ℕ∞))
    (Λ : Type (u + 1)) [CommRing Λ] [Finite Λ] (hΛ : ((ell ^ N : ℕ) : Λ) = 0) :
    ∀ q : ℤ, q < 2 →
      IsZero (((DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor _ q).obj
        ((sectionsWithSupport (ModuleCat.{u + 1} Λ) i.openComplement.ι).rightDerivedFunctor.obj
          ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor _ 0).obj
            (AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.finiteEtaleTateSheaf Λ (ell ^ N) T hΛ 1))))) := by
  intro q hq
  by_cases hneg : q < 0
  · have hGE := CategoryTheory.Functor.isGE_rightDerivedFunctor_obj_singleFunctor
      (sectionsWithSupport (ModuleCat.{u + 1} Λ) i.openComplement.ι)
      (AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.finiteEtaleTateSheaf Λ (ell ^ N) T hΛ 1)
    exact (DerivedCategory.isGE_iff _ 0).mp hGE q hneg
  · have hq01 : q = 0 ∨ q = 1 := by omega
    have hstandard : ∀ {Y G : Scheme.{u}}
        (aY : Y ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [IsSeparated aY] [LocallyOfFiniteType aY]
        [QuasiCompact aY]
        (j : G ⟶ AffineSpace (ULift.{u} (Fin 1)) Y) [IsOpenImmersion j]
        (hj : Set.range j.base =
          (Set.range (AffineSpace.zeroSection (ULift.{u} (Fin 1)) Y).base)ᶜ),
        ∀ r : ℤ, r < 2 → IsZero (((DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor _ r).obj
          ((sectionsWithSupport (ModuleCat.{u + 1} Λ) j).rightDerivedFunctor.obj
            ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor _ 0).obj
              (AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.finiteEtaleTateSheaf Λ (ell ^ N)
                (AffineSpace (ULift.{u} (Fin 1)) Y) (by simpa using hΛ) 1))))) := by
      intro Y G aY hsep hlft hqc j hopen hj r hr
      exact isZero_homology_rightDerivedSectionsWithSupport_standard_pair
        ell N hell hell_unit hN aY j hj Λ hΛ r hr
    rcases hq01 with rfl | rfl
    · exact isZero_homology_rightDerivedSectionsWithSupport_of_smooth_divisor_of_standard_pair
        ell N hell hell_unit hN b v n i hcodim Λ hΛ hstandard 0 (by omega)
    · exact isZero_homology_rightDerivedSectionsWithSupport_of_smooth_divisor_of_standard_pair
        ell N hell hell_unit hN b v n i hcodim Λ hΛ hstandard 1 (by omega)


end AlgebraicGeometry.Etale
